                                                "sense_id": "ad3bbd70-a240-3b40-a2da-b589075008f4",
                                                "text": "As from our beds, we doe oft cast our eyes, / Cleane linnen yeelds a shirt before we rise, / Which is a garment shifting in condition; / And in the canting tongue is a commission."
